#### 8. "What do you think of the Thalmor?"

**Alenawe (Early):** "They are doing the work that needs doing."
**Alenawe (Mid):** "They are doing work. I am no longer certain it is the work that needs doing."
**Alenawe (Late):** "They have confused the long view with the only view. That is a different kind of mistake."

**Followup 1 [Curious] — "Explain."** [+2]
- Early: "I would rather not."
- Mid: *[abridged from draft]* "From their point of view, they are taking what worked about Altmer society and trimming what no longer served. Suffering now, infrastructure later. In three hundred years no one remembers Dacius the farmer."
- Late: "The danger of a long-lived species is the calcification of identity. Institutions have the same problem. So do I, presumably. That is the part that concerns me."

**Followup 2 [Dismissal] — "They're monsters. Everyone knows it."** [-1, but gates a Late variant]
- Early: "That is not a useful frame."
- Mid: "Calling something a monster removes the obligation to understand it. I find that suspicious."
- Late: "…The Justiciars discredit the Council more than any of you ever could. I am aware. I am not going to say it twice."

